This directory contains the openapi spec files used during the generation of the java client code for tapis-client-java.

It is updated as part of the build (mvn clean install) and execution of release-versions.sh script.

The release-versions.sh script is typically only run during an official build of the repo,
but it can be run manually.

The updated openapi spec files here should only be added to git and pushed to the repo as part
of the official build and release which typically happens during execution of the jenkins job:

   TapisJava->2_Release->Shared->release-client-java-local-nexus

Maintaining a copy of these files here as part of a formal deployment release build is
intended to make it easier to reproduce a specific build.
For example, as part of a hot-fix for a service it may be necessary to update an
openapi spec file or the tapis-client-java code which would mean being able to
run a build of tapis-client-java starting with the original dependencies.

Original dependencies include the tapis-bom repo and the openapi spec files used
as part of the build for tapis-client-java.

This directory contains the spec files for the java based services. These files typically come directly from the
respective git repositories (e.g., tapis-project/openapi-systems/SystemsAPI.yaml)

Services Apps, Files, Jobs, Meta, Notifications

The directory also contains the original and processed spec files for other services.
The *.yml files are the originals and typically come directly from the respective git repositories
(e.g. tapis-project/globus-proxy/dev/service/resources/openapi_v3.yml)
The *.json files are generated by converting from the yml file. See gen_spec.sh.

Services: auth, globusproxy, tenants, tokens
